#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Ask the planning store questions, as a product owner would.

WHAT THIS IS FOR
The planning data is only worth collecting if somebody can interrogate it in
the terms they actually think in — "how is the sprint going", "what did that
story really cost", "how much of this sprint was rework the tester found".
This is the command behind the `planning` chat skill, so those questions can
be asked in chat rather than by writing MongoDB queries by hand.

`schema` and `query` exist for the agent rather than for a human: the skill
tells it to read the schema first, then compose its own query for anything the
canned reports do not cover. That is what makes the store USABLE by openclaw
instead of merely written to by it.

Every report degrades rather than fails. The store may not be provisioned yet,
in which case this says so plainly instead of raising — writes spool locally
and flush later, so "no data yet" is a normal state and not an error to be
alarmed by.

Usage:
    planning status                  is the store reachable, how far behind
    planning schema                  the document shapes, for composing queries
    planning sprint [<n>]            one sprint: commitment, scope growth, cost
    planning velocity [--last N]     completed points per sprint
    planning story <owner/repo>#<n>  everything about one story
    planning deploys [--last N]      what the tester tested, and what it cost
    planning rework [<n>]            how much of a sprint was tester findings
    planning query '<json filter>'   raw find, or --pipeline for an aggregation
"""

from __future__ import annotations

